  "answer": "The study confirmed four of the five hard cases it was asked for, each on a different scene. It did not show that sideways plan error causes any of them, because every confirmed case is at 0 m bias. Two scenes fail at their recorded speed with no bias at all (S22, S7), and two fail at 1.2x speed with no bias (S9, S17). The usual failure is the policy braking hard for no clear reason and steering left out of its lane, either into a car in the next lane or off the left edge of the road. Triage puts every failure on the policy. The search never reached the corners the plan named: no bias beyond \u00b10.1 m and no speed below 1.0x was run. Two more caveats: every failure on scene 05f35348 (S7) is flagged as a possible simulator artifact, and the fifth scene (09a95ffa, S12/S13) was not confirmed.",
